// A water wheel stores power in a counterweight. A reservoir drains through a slot down a stepped channel; an
// undershot wheel stands a tile over the third step, its bottom paddles in the stream. Its gear shakes a shaker
// screen beside it and, by a shaft up to the roof and a gear there, turns a counterweight's drum. The weight
// starts low. Before the water arrives, the falling weight alone shakes the screen. While the stream runs the
// wheel gives several hundred watts: the screen shakes and the spare power winds the weight up. When the
// reservoir has run dry the wheel stops, and the weight falls again and keeps the screen shaking.
map
############################################################
############################################################
#............#.............*...............................#
#............#.............j...............................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww#.............j..............@................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww#.............j..........######################
#wwwwwwwwwwww#.............j..........######################
#wwwwwwwwwwww#.............j...............................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww#.............j...............................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww#.............j...............................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww..............j...............................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww..............j...............................#
#wwwwwwwwwwww..............j...............................#
##############.............**H.............................#
####################.......OO..............................#
##########################.................................#
################################...........................#
######################################.....................#
######################################.....................#
######################################.....................#
######################################.....................#
######################################.....................#
######################################.....................#
############################################################
end
give Counterweight 1
place 2 -16 -2 Counterweight           // its drum under the roof, beside the gear there
expect 3 weights == 1
set 4 weight 8                         // let it down 2 m on its rope
expect 5 weighty > 10.9
expect 300 turning:-15,9 == 1          // no water yet: the falling weight turns the train...
expect 300 shaking:-13,9 == 1          // ...and shakes the screen
expect 300 supply:-15,9 < 20
expect 300 weighty > 11
expect 600 supply:-15,9 > 300          // the stream reaches the wheel: hundreds of watts
expect 600 weighty < 9                 // winding the weight up
expect 900 weighty < 5
expect 1200 supply:-15,9 < 20          // the reservoir has run dry: the wheel is still...
expect 1200 turning:-15,9 == 1         // ...and the weight carries the train
expect 1200 shaking:-13,9 == 1
expect 1200 weighty > 4.28             // falling again
saveload 1210
expect 1211 weights == 1
expect 1211 weighty > 4.28
